# TheCoder Extra Docs Maintenance

Before doing deeper repo exploration for TheCoder-specific work, check `.cursor/extra-docs/README.md` and the most relevant topic note.

When a change affects behavior, settings, retry logic, image handling, model selection, or other TheCoder UX, update the matching doc in `.cursor/extra-docs/` in the same change.

Keep those notes short and high-signal:

- explain the current behavior
- list the important file paths
- record the reason for the approach
- avoid long repo-wide re-explanations

If the implementation changes, update the docs first or alongside the code so future work can reuse the summary instead of re-reading the entire repo.
